WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.804 --> 00:00:11.950
OLIVIA: Hello, Little Fox readers, and thanks for tuning in to another edition of People in the

2
00:00:11.951 --> 00:00:16.288
News . I hope you've got your seat belts on because . . . Vroom! We're

3
00:00:16.289 --> 00:00:20.211
going to be traveling at very high speeds today! BEN: That's right, Olivia! Today's person in the

4
00:00:20.212 --> 00:00:29.196
news is the most famous female race car driver in the world—an American named Danica Patrick.

5
00:00:29.197 --> 00:00:36.696
She's the first woman ever to win a major IndyCar championship, and she's set some other pretty

6
00:00:36.697 --> 00:00:41.765
amazing records for female drivers. In fact, lots of fans think she's changed the sport of race

7
00:00:41.766 --> 00:00:50.855
car driving forever. Danica was born on March 25, 1982, and grew up mostly in the

8
00:00:50.856 --> 00:00:58.163
state of Illinois, about 160 kilometers from Chicago. In their spare time, Danica's parents enjoyed being around

9
00:00:58.164 --> 00:01:04.663
fast vehicles like snowmobiles, motorcycles, and cars. In fact, they even met at a race—a snowmobile event

10
00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:08.685
where Danica's mother was working as a mechanic. Danica got her own start in racing when

11
00:01:08.686 --> 00:01:14.332
she was around ten years old. Her sister, Brooke, wanted to try go-kart racing, so the whole

12
00:01:14.333 --> 00:01:22.317
family went along to the track. Brooke didn't enjoy the sport much, but Danica loved it—even

13
00:01:22.318 --> 00:01:30.158
though she crashed into a wall while driving forty kilometers per hour! Despite the crash she knew

14
00:01:30.159 --> 00:01:35.307
how to read the go-kart's tachometer right away, and she had sharp instincts when it came to

15
00:01:35.308 --> 00:01:43.139
correcting her mistakes. Her parents instantly sensed that their daughter had a special gift for driving.

16
00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:51.721
Danica spent the next five years racing in go-kart competitions, traveling around the country to participate in

17
00:01:51.722 --> 00:01:56.117
important races. She was just 12 when she won her first national go-karting championship, and soon she

18
00:01:56.118 --> 00:02:01.041
realized that she wanted to be a race car driver one day. OLIVIA: So when did

19
00:02:01.042 --> 00:02:06.611
Danica start racing cars instead of go-karts? BEN: Well, when she was 16, Danica decided to start

20
00:02:06.612 --> 00:02:12.020
racing Formula cars—those are race cars with open wheels outside the car's main body and a

21
00:02:12.021 --> 00:02:14.930
single seat for the driver. Danica knew this would be difficult, especially since it meant leaving high

22
00:02:14.931 --> 00:02:18.846
school and moving to England, where many drivers launch their careers. After obtaining a high school equivalency

23
00:02:18.847 --> 00:02:24.343
diploma in the United States, she made the move across the Atlantic, living in a small

24
00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:32.343
town about seventy kilometers from London. Danica was doing something very exciting—driving over 320 kilometers per hour

25
00:02:32.344 --> 00:02:36.157
in a series of challenging races—but she later described this as the loneliest time in her life.

26
00:02:36.158 --> 00:02:41.576
As the only girl on the team, she was ignored and teased by her male teammates.

27
00:02:41.577 --> 00:02:46.905
Many of the others around the track—coaches, mechanics, even the owner of her racing team—also dismissed her

28
00:02:46.906 --> 00:02:52.491
as a lightweight girl who wasn't strong or tough enough to last in the sport. But

29
00:02:52.492 --> 00:02:57.972
gradually the difficult situation taught Danica something very valuable for her career: how to stay unemotional and

30
00:02:57.973 --> 00:03:01.905
calm during competition. In 2000 Danica moved up to the next level in Formula racing, and entered

31
00:03:01.906 --> 00:03:10.638
the Formula Ford Festival, an important event in motorsports. She won second place there, the best-ever

32
00:03:10.639 --> 00:03:16.547
finish for an American, male or female. Gradually Danica began to attract sponsors—people who could support her

33
00:03:16.548 --> 00:03:24.548
career with money, equipment, and other resources. In 2002 she moved back to the United States

34
00:03:24.549 --> 00:03:32.535
and began racing IndyCars, the American version of open-wheeled race cars. OLIVIA: So did she ever qualify

35
00:03:32.536 --> 00:03:39.700
for the really famous IndyCar race—the Indianapolis 500? BEN: Yes. In 2005 she qualified to compete in

36
00:03:39.701 --> 00:03:45.953
that race, better known as the Indy 500. Believe it or not, Olivia, Danica was only

37
00:03:45.954 --> 00:03:51.198
the fourth woman ever to do this. In fact, only about thirty years earlier, women weren't even

38
00:03:51.199 --> 00:03:58.426
allowed in the garage area or in the pits with the drivers! Danica started out strong in

39
00:03:58.427 --> 00:04:03.917
her first Indy 500, taking the lead in the 57th lap—the first time a female driver

40
00:04:03.918 --> 00:04:08.430
had ever been in front of all the other cars. She stayed in the lead for 19

41
00:04:08.431 --> 00:04:14.420
laps. But soon she had to make a pit stop for fuel. When the 200-lap race

42
00:04:14.421 --> 00:04:18.837
ended, Danica was in fourth place. That was the best performance ever by a woman, and Danica

43
00:04:18.838 --> 00:04:26.090
was named the 2005 IndyCar Rookie of the Year. Three years later she became the first woman

44
00:04:26.091 --> 00:04:34.988
ever to win an Indy race when she shot through the finish line first at the

45
00:04:34.989 --> 00:04:43.998
Indy Japan 300. Around 2011 Danica decided to leave the IndyCar circuit and join NASCAR (National Association

46
00:04:43.999 --> 00:04:50.225
for Stock Car Auto Racing). As a NASCAR driver, she has had the best finish for a

47
00:04:50.226 --> 00:04:55.058
woman and she continues to break records. Many people credit her with bringing lots of new

48
00:04:55.059 --> 00:04:59.554
excitement to NASCAR racing. Danica's successes have also turned her into a very wealthy woman. Today she

49
00:04:59.555 --> 00:05:06.554
not only drives cars, she models and even acts, appearing in music videos and on TV

50
00:05:06.555 --> 00:05:12.458
shows. She has dozens of sponsors, and is one of the biggest earners among all professional drivers.

51
00:05:12.459 --> 00:05:18.686
She definitely attracts criticism too, with some people saying that her racing record isn't that impressive; she's

52
00:05:18.687 --> 00:05:25.366
only succeeded because she's a female—a very good-looking female—who knows how to market herself. But Danica

53
00:05:25.367 --> 00:05:34.020
is determined not to let this criticism get in her way. She's very confident in her own

54
00:05:34.021 --> 00:05:40.782
driving talent and proud of her success. She's also quite proud of the fact that she's helped

55
00:05:40.783 --> 00:05:46.017
women gain recognition in a sport that has always been dominated by men. Thanks to Danica,

56
00:05:46.018 --> 00:05:51.421
female drivers are taken a lot more seriously today at the track. OLIVIA: Wow! It sounds like

57
00:05:51.422 --> 00:05:55.348
it's been quite a ride for Danica Patrick so far. Thanks for telling us more about

58
00:05:55.349 --> 00:06:02.507
her fast-paced career, Ben. See you soon, Little Fox readers, to meet another person in the news.

